ept":"sga","tag":"SellingGeneralAndAdministrativeExpense","value":"133384000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"depreciation","tag":"Depreciation","value":"1799000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"net_income","tag":"NetIncomeLoss","value":"29446000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"cfo","tag":"NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities","value":"18807000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"receivables","tag":"AccountsReceivableNetCurrent","value":"53755000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"current_assets","tag":"AssetsCurrent","value":"96310000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"ppe","tag":"PropertyPlantAndEquipmentNet","value":"9475000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"assets","tag":"Assets","value":"135913000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"},{"cik":"1376339","company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","concept":"current_liabilities","tag":"LiabilitiesCurrent","value":"26777000","accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29"}]},"company":{"attrs":{"cik":1376339,"company":"MiMedx Group","fy_end":"2015-12-31","activeRevision":"a4e168d4e009","liveRevision":""}},"filings":[{"attrs":{"accn":"0001376339-15-000040","filed":"2015-03-13","cik":1376339,"company":"MiMedx Group","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1376339/000137633915000040/0001376339-15-000040-index.htm","form":"10-K"}},{"attrs":{"accn":"0001376339-16-000138","filed":"2016-02-29","cik":1376339,"company":"MiMedx Group","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1376339/000137633916000138/mdxg-20151231x10k.htm","form":"10-K"}}],"findings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1376339_2015-12-31","revisionId":"a4e168d4e009","sampleIndex":0,"findingIndex":1,"management_says":"Revenue growth reflects healthy demand (implied by lack of disclosed timing/terms changes in MD&A).","numbers_show":"Revenue growth decelerated each quarter (+108%, +79%, +46%, +31%) while receivables growth accelerated (+64%, +92%, +101%, +102%) and DSO deteriorated sharply in H2 (Q3: 63→87, Q4: 61→94) (E25-E28). Beneish M-score flags manipulation risk (-1.23 > -1.78 threshold) driven by high sales growth index (1.58), DSRI (1.27), and asset quality index (1.34) (E29).","fit":"does not fit","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29"],"verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers"}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1376339_2015-12-31","revisionId":"a4e168d4e009","sampleIndex":2,"findingIndex":1,"management_says":"Implicitly attributes revenue growth to healthy demand (no explicit causal driver cited in MD&A excerpts provided).","numbers_show":"Quarterly pattern shows H2 revenue growth slowing sharply while receivables and DSO spike — Q4 revenue +31% but receivables +102% and DSO 61→94 days (E28). This divergence suggests a meaningful portion of Q4 revenue came from shipment timing or extended terms rather than underlying demand. Beneish M-score flagged (DSRI=1.27, SGI=1.58, AQI=1.34) consistent with aggressive revenue recognition or channel loading (E29).","fit":"does not fit","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29"],"verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers"}}],"rulings":[{"attrs":{"caseId":"1376339_2015-12-31","revisionId":"a4e168d4e009","sampleIndex":0,"rulingIndex":1,"finding_index":1,"ruling":"unverified","reason":"Management's implied claim that revenue growth reflects healthy demand is not corroborated by reported numbers; quarterly signals show revenue growth decelerating (+108%, +79%, +46%, +31%) while receivables growth accelerated (+64%, +92%, +101%, +102%) and DSO deteriorated sharply in H2 (Q3: 63→87, Q4: 61→94) (E25-E28), and the Beneish M-score flags manipulation risk (E29). The pack lacks segment or channel data to verify the demand quality or quantify any mix shift.","evidence":["E23","E25","E26","E27","E28","E29","E30","E32"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":1,"innocent_explanation":"The quarterly revenue growth deceleration (E25-E28: +108%, +79%, +46%, +31%) is consistent with lapping easier year-ago comparisons after rapid early-2015 growth. The accelerating receivables growth and DSO deterioration in H2 (E25-E28) could reflect a strategic shift to expand distributor relationships (which have longer payment terms per E32) to drive future growth, or quarter-end timing of large distributor orders. The Beneish M-score (E29) flags risk due to high sales growth (SGI=1.58) and receivables growth (DSRI=1.27), which are characteristic of high-growth companies and do not prove manipulation. The pack contains no disclosure of payment term changes (E30, E32) but also no evidence of fraudulent revenue recognition.","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29","E30","E32"],"support":"outside the pack"},"final_verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers","confidence":0.85}},{"attrs":{"caseId":"1376339_2015-12-31","revisionId":"a4e168d4e009","sampleIndex":2,"rulingIndex":1,"finding_index":1,"ruling":"does not fit","reason":"The implicit claim that revenue growth reflects healthy demand is contradicted by the H2 divergence: Q4 revenue grew only 31% while receivables grew 102% and DSO jumped from 61 to 94 days (E28). This pattern — receivables and DSO spiking as revenue growth decelerates — is inconsistent with pure demand-driven growth. The Beneish M-score flag (E29) signals unusual accruals but does not, by itself, prove manipulation; however, no reported driver (segment mix, new contracts, payment-term changes) appears in the evidence pack to corroborate a benign explanation. The defender's 'timing effect' interpretation is plausible but rests on facts outside the pack (no channel-level data, no distributor agreements).","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29"],"rebuttal":{"finding_index":1,"innocent_explanation":"The H2 divergence between slowing revenue growth and spiking receivables/DSO is a timing effect visible in the quarterly signals: Q4 revenue grew 31% while receivables grew 102% and DSO jumped from 61 to 94 days (E28), indicating a concentration of late-quarter shipments with extended terms. This pattern is consistent with a one-time channel stocking event, not aggressive revenue recognition. The Beneish M-score flag (E29) is a statistical indicator that often triggers for high-growth companies with changing receivables patterns and does not, by itself, evidence manipulation. The revenue growth deceleration reflects tougher year-over-year comparisons as 2014 H2 growth was already elevated.","evidence":["E25","E26","E27","E28","E29"],"support":"numbers"},"final_verdict":"explanation does not fit the numbers","confidence":0.85}}],"audit":[{"seq":29,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:ingest:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":114,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"evidence:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29 (evidence)","kind":"upsertEntity"},{"seq":115,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"filing:accn:0001376339-15-000040 -[supports]-> evidence:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29","kind":"relate"},{"seq":116,"actor":"evidence-pack","summary":"filing:accn:0001376339-16-000138 -[supports]-> evidence:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29","kind":"relate"},{"seq":138,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29 -[supports]-> finding:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:s0:f1","kind":"relate"},{"seq":164,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29 -[cites]-> ruling:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:s0:r1","kind":"relate"},{"seq":237,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29 -[supports]-> finding:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:s2:f1","kind":"relate"},{"seq":261,"actor":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b","summary":"evidence:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:E29 -[cites]-> ruling:1376339_2015-12-31:a4e168d4e009:s2:r1","kind":"relate"}]}